From bf3fc1102be6a276b8c41929fd778e37af86c864 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:01:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] SimAntics: feature switches and route/queue diagnostics

- VMFeatures: per-process switches for Simitone's behaviour changes,
  set by the client from its settings (Shimmy forwards to
  VMShimmyPlanner.Enabled). Every later change gets one.
- Diagnostics.VMDiagnostics: records, per avatar, recent route events
  (begin, goal, no room route, wait, timeout, collision, soft/hard fail,
  arrived) and why every queued action left the queue (completed,
  completed false, cancelled, check tree failed at start, callee deleted,
  queue skipped, interrupted, reset because the running action's object
  died, exception). Dump() writes a readable report. Recording only, no
  behaviour change; transient (VMEntity.Diagnostics is not saved).
- Hooks in VMRoutingFrame and VMThread at the existing fail/end points.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019q6m8f542cVUMKg755aFtZ
